      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 228.44,
      "end_seconds": 230.14,
      "duration_seconds": 1.7,
      "text": "nope no vomiting"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 231.97,
      "end_seconds": 236.85,
      "duration_seconds": 4.88,
      "text": "Actually doctor I did notice vomiting. He doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 238.59,
      "end_seconds": 246.01,
      "duration_seconds": 7.42,
      "text": "hmm, no, I don't think I did. Maybe a a little, I'm not sure"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 247.2,
      "end_seconds": 256.63,
      "duration_seconds": 9.43,
      "text": "alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. On the cardiac side, anything I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 257.2,
      "end_seconds": 262.01,
      "duration_seconds": 4.81,
      "text": "My heart's been fine, as far as I know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 263.61,
      "end_seconds": 267.93,
      "duration_seconds": 4.32,
      "text": "let me get the readings out of the way"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 281.53,
      "end_seconds": 283.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "bear with me while this finishes.."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 301.74,
      "end_seconds": 307.89,
      "duration_seconds": 6.15,
      "text": "okay: pulse 103 temp 38.5 degrees. And pressure 124 over 79 saturation 98 percent"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 308.53,
      "end_seconds": 309.87,
      "duration_seconds": 1.34,
      "text": "Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 314.66,
      "end_seconds": 319.1,
      "duration_seconds": 4.44,
      "text": "They help me see the whole picture, more shortly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 320.88,
      "end_seconds": 323.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.71,
      "text": "let's move on to the examination"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 324.54,
      "end_seconds": 327.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "Take a deep breath for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 334.2,
      "end_seconds": 339.18,
      "duration_seconds": 4.98,
      "text": "The pulses at the ankle are weak but I can feel them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 340.24,
      "end_seconds": 342.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "take a deep breath for me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 361.32,
      "end_seconds": 367.97,
      "duration_seconds": 6.65,
      "text": "There is a two-centimetre ulcer on the ball of the right foot with redness around it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 373.01,
      "end_seconds": 374.77,
      "duration_seconds": 1.76,
      "text": "That's the examination finished."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 386.99,
      "end_seconds": 399.33,
      "duration_seconds": 12.34,
      "text": "so where does that leave us? This looks most like an infected diabetic foot ulcer it could also be pressure damage, so we'll keep that open"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 400.4,
      "end_seconds": 404.01,
      "duration_seconds": 3.61,
      "text": "actually, what are the odds it's serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 405.12,
      "end_seconds": 422.32,
      "duration_seconds": 17.2,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like an infected diabetic foot ulcer, but I'd like to confirm. Just to be sure I understood. You've had a sore on the bottom of your foot, and no confusion or chest pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 423.31,
      "end_seconds": 424.01,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "exactly"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 426.07,
      "end_seconds": 459.83,
      "duration_seconds": 33.76,
      "text": "we should do blood tests for infection. A foot X-ray is what I'd like next, for ulcer. I'd like you to take amoxicillin/clavulanic acid, 625 milligrams, three times a day, for seven days. You take it by mouth. That should help with foot infection. Keep the weight off that foot and keep the dressing dry. If the redness spreads or you feel unwell with a fever, that's the point to come in urgently"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 460.49,
      "end_seconds": 461.41,
      "duration_seconds": 0.92,
      "text": "I understand."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 462.87,
      "end_seconds": 466.2,
      "duration_seconds": 3.33,
      "text": "let's review you after the swab result"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 467.12,
      "end_seconds": 468.65,
      "duration_seconds": 1.53,
      "text": "yes, that's manageable"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 469.21,
      "end_seconds": 472.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "Have I covered everything you wanted?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 474.18,
